<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Unknown entry from the determinant</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(M = {@Mk@}\).</p><p>(a) Find the value of \(k\) for which \(M\) has no inverse.</p><div>\(k = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Under \(M\), a shape of area \({@A0@}\) square units has an image of area \({@A0*s@}\) square units. Find the two possible values of \(k\).</p><div>\(k = \) [[input:ans2]] or \(k = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\det M = {@dk@}\).</p><p>(a) No inverse means \(\det M = 0\): \({@dk@} = 0\), so \(k = {@k0@}\).</p><p>(b) The area scale factor is \({@A0*s@} \div {@A0@} = {@s@}\), and it equals \(|\det M|\). So \({@dk@} = {@s@}\), giving \(k = {@k1@}\), or \({@dk@} = {@-s@}\), giving \(k = {@k2@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: find an unknown entry from the determinant. Source: original. k0, k1, k2 are integers, k1 # k2 and neither equals k0; the image-area values kA differ from both. */
klist: [[6,4,1,3,2],[2,3,1,3,3],[6,1,1,7,2],[-2,-1,1,9,2],[3,2,1,3,4],[4,-2,-2,4,2],[5,2,-2,6,2],[-4,-1,1,3,4],[5,1,1,9,2],[6,-3,1,2,2]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
p: klist[ix][1]; q: klist[ix][2]; r: klist[ix][3]; s: klist[ix][4]; A0: klist[ix][5];
Mk: matrix([k,p],[q,r]);
dk: r*k-p*q;
k0: p*q/r; k1: (p*q+s)/r; k2: (p*q-s)/r;
mk0: -k0;
kA1: (p*q+s*A0)/r; kA2: (p*q-s*A0)/r;
tw0: k0+1; tw1: k1+1; tw2: k2+1;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
